 r"I am writing to apply for the AI \& Business Solutions Graduate position at Shanly Group. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have spotted processes that could be done better, built working AI tools and automated workflows to fix them, and made sure the people using them found them simple and trustworthy.",

 r"What attracts me most to this role is that the work has a visible end point: tools that busy colleagues across the Group actually use, rather than recommendations about what could be done. The posting asks for someone who enjoys making things work and who has already built things, and that is exactly how I have approached AI so far. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK my supervisor asked me to configure a merchant campaign by hand, matching the right settings to each merchant. After working through a few examples I could see the logic, so I proposed building an AI agent with Claude Code to do it, with a validation step to check its accuracy. My supervisor was sceptical at first, but I delivered it before the same-day deadline and it cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent. I also build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to track their work. The main lesson was that a tool only creates value once the people using it trust it.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a medical AI project for a pharmaceutical client. I built a Python pipeline that connected six AI models through their APIs and automatically produced and scored more than 2,400 responses, and a workflow that turned 4,800 free-text patient consultation threads into structured data. I also turned the client's requirements into a benchmark that they adopted as their acceptance standard, and explained the results to clinical and business colleagues who were not technical.",

 r"I also build things in my own time to learn new tools. For my MSc dissertation I turned complex cardiovascular risk models into an interactive Streamlit app so non-specialists could explore the results, and more recently I built a question-answering agent over NHS health pages with Claude Code. I pick up new tools quickly, and I would be keen to bring the same approach to Microsoft 365, Copilot and the Power Platform.",

 r"I would bring Shanly Group hands-on experience of building AI agents and automated workflows, strong Python and data skills, an eye for making tools simple for non-technical users, and the ability to explain technical ideas clearly. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship, and I am happy to work from the Beaconsfield office.",

 r"Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience in AI, automation and building practical tools could help Shanly Group work more simply and efficiently.",
